he tubes every 30 min. The samples were reduced in 5 mM tris(2-carboxyethyl)phosphine (TCEP) for 30 min at room temperature and alkylated in 10 mM methyl methanethiosulfonate (MMTS) for 30 min at room temperature. A second digestion was performed with 0.3 µg Pierce MS grade Trypsin (Thermo Fisher Scientific) at 37°C overnight. Next morning the digested samples were removed from beads with a magnetic stand and the beads were washed twice with 50 µl 50 mM TEAB that were pooled with the supernatants. Digested peptides were labelled using Tandem Mass Tag reagents (TMTpro, Thermo Fisher Scientific) according to the manufacturer´s instructions. The combined set was pre-fractionated into 5 and 10 fractions using Pierce High pH Reversed-Phase Peptide Fractionation Kit (Thermo Scientific) according to the manufacturer’s protocol. The fractions were dried in a vacuum centrifuge and reconstituted in 3% acetonitrile, 0.1% formic acid for analysis. The fractions were analyzed on an Orbitrap Fusion™ Lumos™ Tribrid™ mass spectrometer interfaced with an Easy-nLC1200 liquid chromatography system (both Thermo Fisher Scientific). Peptides were trapped on an Acclaim Pepmap 100 C18 trap column (100 μm x 2 cm, particle size 5 μm, Thermo Fischer Scientific) and separated on an in-house packed analytical column i.d. 75 μm, particle size 3 μm, Reprosil-Pur C18, Dr. Maisch, length 35 cm using a linear gradient from 5% to 33% B over 77 min followed by an increase to 100% B for 3 min, and 100% B for 10 min at a flow of 300 nL/min. Solvent A was 0.2% formic acid and solvent B was 80% acetonitrile, 0.2% formic acid. Precursor ion mass spectra were acquired at 120 000 resolution and MS/MS analysis was performed in a data-dependent multinotch mode where CID spectra of the most intense precursor ions were recorded in the ion trap with collision energy setting of 30 for 3 s (‘top speed’ setting). Precursors were isolated in the quadrupole with a 0.7 m/z isolation window, charge states 2 to 7 were selected for fragmentation, dynamic exclusion was set to 45 s and 10 ppm. MS3 spectra for reporter ion quantitation were recorded at 50 000 resolution with HCD fragmentation at collision energy of and 55 using the synchronous precursor selection.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
